    "changes":  [
                    {
                        "field":  "rule",
                        "table":  "articles",
                        "key":  {
                                    "provision_id":  "A132"
                                },
                        "proposed":  "FINAL-ARCHITECTURE:decision-core,permission-core,runtime-core,automation-core and xingcheng-assistant are the five peer cores; Xingcheng is a separate native-model identity. RESPONSIBILITY:decision-core owns policy and acceptance decisions;permission-core owns identity,scope,permission,directory and security enforcement;runtime-core owns startup,process lifecycle and governed execution;automation-core owns authorized workflow scheduling and synchronization;xingcheng-assistant owns inspection,notification and user permission presentation. EXECUTION:C and Rust own deterministic runtime and lifecycle hot paths,C++ owns inference,audit,test execution and resource governance,CSharp owns application/API/workflow/test orchestration,FSharp owns business rules and high-correctness analysis,Go owns high-concurrency network/file/batch work. CONTRACT:all cross-core work uses registered versioned contracts,bounded execution,permission checks,receipts and fail-closed outcomes. PYTHON-RETIREMENT:Python is fully retired throughout the project under B4/B73/B74; ACTIVE-ROLE:none; normal and on-demand Python process count zero; no governance semantic adapter,training job,core host,coordinator or execution fallback is permitted."
                    },
                    {
                        "field":  "prohibition",
                        "table":  "articles",
                        "key":  {
                                    "provision_id":  "A132"
                                },
                        "proposed":  "FORBID:sovereign-to-engine-transition-state+Python-active-role-or-residency+Python-governance-adapter-or-training-job+Python-core-host-or-coordinator-or-execution-fallback+duplicate-core-owner+module-self-authorization+unregistered-cross-core-route+unbounded-execution"
                    },
                    {
                        "field":  "rule",
                        "table":  "articles",
                        "key":  {
                                    "provision_id":  "B4"
                                },
                        "proposed":  "FINAL-PYTHON-RESPONSIBILITY:Python is fully retired throughout the project under B73/B74; ACTIVE-ROLE:none. RESIDENCY:normal and on-demand Python process count is zero. The former request-scoped governance semantic adapter and Xingcheng JAX/XLA training responsibilities are abolished without exception. SOURCE-VALIDITY:no Python source root,module,package or dependency is conforming; retired Python is not a supported compatibility or fallback path. OWNERSHIP:current responsibilities resolve only to registered non-Python owners under B76/B166 and the applicable domain special law. TEST-AUDIT:Python,pytest and Python validators have zero formal responsibility in testing,audit,verification,release and push flows. REPLACEMENT:any successor capability requires a separately registered non-Python owner amendment."
                    },
                    {
                        "field":  "prohibition",
                        "table":  "articles",
                        "key":  {
                                    "provision_id":  "B4"
                                },
                        "proposed":  "FORBID:Python-active-role-or-residency+Python-governance-semantic-adapter+Python-JAX-XLA-training-job+Python-source-root-module-package-or-dependency+Python-test-audit-verification-release-push+Python-runtime-fallback+retired-role-restoration"
                    }
                ],
    "acceptance":  {
                       "expected_state":  "A132 and B4 consistently declare complete Python retirement with zero active roles and zero normal/on-demand processes, matching B73/B74.",
